menu "ExecuTorch runner"

    config ET_BENCH_MEM
        bool "Memory bandwidth and weight-tier rate rows at boot (hardware only)"
        default n
        help
            Builds main.cpp's bench_memory and the weight tiers' kernel-rate
            rows (bench_tiers.cpp) into the firmware and runs them at boot,
            before the model. The same as -DET_BENCH_MEM=1, for a build whose
            command line is fixed: run_story_hardware.py --sdkconfig-extra
            sdkconfig.bench.defaults builds the story with them, in a build
            directory of its own. Emulated flash is RAM, so the rows mean
            nothing under QEMU.

endmenu
